@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · AZRAEL · STANDING" m="TKC: TL · TR · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:mountain}"
# The record's version and the true one
rec:
On the record | Dead since 2100 of a medical event (TL). "A sudden medical event" is the phrase the Empire uses for Petra too (TR).
In fact | Alive, in a Mountain community whose patriarch owes the Vane family a debt that predates the Trials Commission by a decade. The Empire doesn't know. Almost no one does (TL).
Where he is | Mountain is where the Empire's least documented and most important work happens, up past Crestfall (DOM). Endurance returns to its lower ranges for the 39th Trial without explanation (TR).
Who knows | Judah, Lyris and two others (TL).
prompt: What he does all day in Mountain, and what he can never do there | fill

@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · AZRAEL · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TL · FR 44; VOL. I · {v1:texts} · {v1:ledger}"
# What he believes
rec:
Who taught him | The Temple's schools, which he out-asked (TL), and after them the ledger.
What he knows | The Covenant of Purpose calls a series of deliberate removals God's order. The ledger calls them something else (TL).
What he believes | OPEN QUESTION: After the ledger, what's left of the faith he was raised in, and what he'd put in its place.
What he'd be arrested for | Being alive (TL).
empire: What the Temple teaches about a man like him
A son of the anointed bloodline is anointed (CR). INTERPRETATION: The Temple has no doctrine for an anointed son who asks what the anointing is built on, so it recorded him as dead.
/end
prompt: What he believes the Covenant of Dissent says | fill

@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · AZRAEL · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 2 OF 2" m="GEN 37.31–35; 1 KGS 17.2–6; 1 KGS 18.4; JER 36.26; LUKE 8.17; JER 36.23"
# The text
rec:
Joseph · Genesis 37 | POSSIBLE: A favored son reported dead to his father, alive in another country (37.31–35). **Where it breaks:** Jacob grieves a lie his other sons told him. In Azrael's family the question is who told the lie (TL).
Elijah at Cherith · 1 Kings 17 | POSSIBLE: Told to hide himself by a brook, and fed there by ravens. **Where it breaks:** Elijah goes back to confront the king. Whether Azrael can is the book.
Obadiah's cave · 1 Kings 18.4 | POSSIBLE: A palace steward who hides a hundred prophets in caves and feeds them with bread and water. INTERPRETATION: The patriarch who owes the Vanes a debt (TL).
Baruch · Jeremiah 36 | POSSIBLE: The scribe of a scroll the king wants destroyed. "But the LORD hid them" (36.26).
tab:
| He'd quote | Never read to him |
| Luke 8.17, "nothing is secret, that shall not be made manifest" | Jeremiah 36.23, a king cutting a scroll with a penknife |
